        "original_id": "f5b23615-e872-5f88-b39f-7d4b7cfe8c61",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Howea, H. forsteriana, Bulbophyllum, Linospadicinae, Linospadix\n- Places: Northern Hemisphere, Africa, southern Asia, Latin America, West Indies, Indian Ocean, Pacific Ocean\n- Industries: palm seed industry, trade in newly germinated seedlings\n\nFacts:\n- Linospadicinae is a subtribe of palm trees that includes the genera Howea and Linospadix.\n- H. forsteriana is commonly grown as an indoor plant in the Northern Hemisphere.\n- The two Howea species form the mainstay of the island's palm seed industry and its trade in newly germinated seedlings.\n- Bulbophyllum is found throughout most of the warmer parts of the world, including Africa, southern Asia, Latin America, the West Indies, and various islands in the Indian and Pacific Oceans.",
